rsgain
------------------------------------------
rsgain (really simple gain) is a ReplayGain 2.0 command line utility for
Windows, macOS, Linux, BSD, and Android. rsgain applies loudness metadata tags
to your files, while leaving the audio stream untouched. A
ReplayGain-compatible player will dynamically adjust the volume of your tagged
files during playback.

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.12-1
  libavcodec63-9.0.2-2
  libavformat63-9.0.2-2
  libavutil61-9.0.2-2
  libebur128_1-1.2.6-1bl3
  libfmt12-12.2.0-1bl1
  libgcc1-14.4.0-1
  libinih0-62-1
  libstdc++6-14.4.0-1
  libswresample7-9.0.2-2
  libtag2-2.3.2-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  binutils-2.47-1
  cmake-4.4.5-1
  cygport-0.37.12-1
  gcc-g++-14.4.0-1
  libavcodec-devel-9.0.2-2
  libavformat-devel-9.0.2-2
  libavutil-devel-9.0.2-2
  libebur128-devel-1.2.6-1bl3
  libfmt-devel-12.2.0-1bl1
  libinih-devel-62-1
  libswresample-devel-9.0.2-2
  libtag-devel-2.3.2-1
  ninja-1.13.2-1

Canonical website:
  https://github.com/complexlogic/rsgain

Canonical download:
  https://github.com/complexlogic/rsgain/archive/refs/tags/v3.8.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack rsgain-3.8-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./rsgain-3.8-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/rsgain-3.8-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/rsgain-3.8-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

